The change (2026-10-20): the kit's projection is right-handed, so a figure drawn in its CAD's frame is
not the CAD's mirror image. In iso-kit.mjs, iso() draws screen x the other way; the lights (extrude's
and lathe.mjs's lightOf, both now from lightAcross) and audit.mjs's cameraBasis turn with it, so the
light stays on the screen's upper left; and topMatrix and sideMatrix keep face text the right way round
(sideMatrix's "left" is now the face across x, the one on the screen's left). The camera sits where it
did. A projection with leftHanded: true draws exactly as Anatomy's does.

The stage 1 steps in reference/run.md are adapted from Anatomy's workflow.

Everything else in this folder is Sprue's own.
